{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_c99b008d74db552cc37541c39f16eb8bdd9f0c8aede342b037ae08b384a0292c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Agent behavior is modeled as AgentProfile entities managed by agent-profile-manager.ts, with system prompts assembled via a prompts system supporting placeholder substitution; subagents are profiles invoked by a parent profile."}],"claim_ids":["clm_c99b008d74db552cc37541c39f16eb8bdd9f0c8aede342b037ae08b384a0292c"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:04:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_c3b68b30a908496abe5ab36586526291","id":"pg_167fe1d30b4a5e78a0c87b882ffaec57","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/hotovo-aider-desk-docs-adr-agent-system-0007-agent-profiles-and-system-7b882ffaec57.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_07758cc2fa085f6b9fec02ce849bc834"],"title":"hotovo/aider-desk/docs/adr/agent-system/0007-agent-profiles-and-system-prompts.md @ cb7ee89bf213","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:04:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_c3b68b30a908496abe5ab36586526291"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_915110b53b566041c048c8578b226d2d84a2347d511aa977e073d9667ab4b760"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: new ADRs follow a template with global sequential numbering, retroactive ADRs may be Accepted only after verification against current source, and Accepted decisions are never edited in place."}],"claim_ids":["clm_915110b53b566041c048c8578b226d2d84a2347d511aa977e073d9667ab4b760"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:04:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_c3b68b30a908496abe5ab36586526291","id":"pg_33082e9c92265baf9e05c85b47e736e5","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/hotovo-aider-desk-docs-adr-template-md-cb7ee89bf213-c85b47e736e5.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_e0e232e556705dd5af8a10f0aa70dc27"],"title":"hotovo/aider-desk/docs/adr/template.md @ cb7ee89bf213","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:04:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_c3b68b30a908496abe5ab36586526291"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_c78f72502626a43e2f4063c55520e33b6b6dc4eb1b2be02e8813858be74c0bf6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The frontend is built with React 19 and Tailwind CSS; the agent runtime depends on the Vercel AI SDK, with MCP support via @ai-sdk/mcp and @modelcontextprotocol/sdk."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ed124be0cfc3618cb36dde9851403ce8fd6d40ce5dece7df95b743bdfd8c52f1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The agent runtime is built on the Vercel AI SDK; SDK message parts are the runtime currency, while persistence uses AiderDesk's own ContextMessage types, converted at the agent boundary in src/main/agent/utils.ts."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f3a4b28ad837cead0e510162283f8474745ef8141638cb2f2abed046a3b4b409"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The ADRs note trade-offs: SDK upgrades can shift part/type shapes requiring a dedicated pass, and MCP connection lifecycle issues (restarts, timeouts, unauthorized states) must be handled robustly across process boundaries."}],"claim_ids":["clm_c78f72502626a43e2f4063c55520e33b6b6dc4eb1b2be02e8813858be74c0bf6","clm_ed124be0cfc3618cb36dde9851403ce8fd6d40ce5dece7df95b743bdfd8c52f1","clm_f3a4b28ad837cead0e510162283f8474745ef8141638cb2f2abed046a3b4b409"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:04:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_c3b68b30a908496abe5ab36586526291","id":"pg_50c401096a15542a84959bf3cf6d7193","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/hotovo-aider-desk-docs-adr-agent-system-0005-vercel-ai-sdk-as-agent-ru-9bf3cf6d7193.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_2cfb556ae44e50a48a8474c2593a3ac4"],"title":"hotovo/aider-desk/docs/adr/agent-system/0005-vercel-ai-sdk-as-agent-runtime.md @ cb7ee89bf213","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:04:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_c3b68b30a908496abe5ab36586526291"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_300fac2017e23e353be305cb27401a8f2c09f52995941a2fee0206d0185c98e3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"MCP is the standard tool boundary: servers connect via stdio or HTTP transports, tools are namespaced as <server><sep><tool>, and every invocation passes through the ApprovalManager."},{"claim_ids":["clm_bd9f650e4c3d85dd5fdb4407f0d16710d10fb56eb61c8da9556d59a8c856aeac"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product features tool approval gates where users approve tools and authorize destructive actions; per the ADRs, all MCP tool invocations route through the ApprovalManager."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c78f72502626a43e2f4063c55520e33b6b6dc4eb1b2be02e8813858be74c0bf6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The frontend is built with React 19 and Tailwind CSS; the agent runtime depends on the Vercel AI SDK, with MCP support via @ai-sdk/mcp and @modelcontextprotocol/sdk."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f3a4b28ad837cead0e510162283f8474745ef8141638cb2f2abed046a3b4b409"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The ADRs note trade-offs: SDK upgrades can shift part/type shapes requiring a dedicated pass, and MCP connection lifecycle issues (restarts, timeouts, unauthorized states) must be handled robustly across process boundaries."}],"claim_ids":["clm_300fac2017e23e353be305cb27401a8f2c09f52995941a2fee0206d0185c98e3","clm_bd9f650e4c3d85dd5fdb4407f0d16710d10fb56eb61c8da9556d59a8c856aeac","clm_c78f72502626a43e2f4063c55520e33b6b6dc4eb1b2be02e8813858be74c0bf6","clm_f3a4b28ad837cead0e510162283f8474745ef8141638cb2f2abed046a3b4b409"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:04:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_c3b68b30a908496abe5ab36586526291","id":"pg_5f486e3af7c25335bfff5e60497f5393","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/hotovo-aider-desk-docs-adr-agent-system-0006-mcp-for-tool-extensibilit-5e60497f5393.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_6eb6a1aaed025462852f9a25d7dea77f"],"title":"hotovo/aider-desk/docs/adr/agent-system/0006-mcp-for-tool-extensibility.md @ cb7ee89bf213","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:04:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_c3b68b30a908496abe5ab36586526291"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_2d4cd98a783a23e48c175d22742ab00c20dec9a496038197f369091daec82af3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the ADR review checklist requires tracing call paths against source, separating current behavior from desired future state, and avoiding absolute security or durability claims unless the code enforces them."},{"claim_ids":["clm_83588e36928427d7e20021b8153c665ff1b59d50beac42fb2faf24404ea9beea"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The ADR set was written retroactively by analyzing the existing codebase, documenting de-facto decisions that are descriptive of current architecture and prescriptive for future changes."},{"claim_ids":["clm_915110b53b566041c048c8578b226d2d84a2347d511aa977e073d9667ab4b760"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: new ADRs follow a template with global sequential numbering, retroactive ADRs may be Accepted only after verification against current source, and Accepted decisions are never edited in place."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9813c92cc8a5d7265e9f2d1e9767c0b515cc229ad39154aebb9da2144e7e5dcf"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: every ADR must include a mandatory 'Guardrails for Agents' section with do/don't rules, and changes conflicting with an ADR require updating the ADR first or changing the approach."}],"claim_ids":["clm_2d4cd98a783a23e48c175d22742ab00c20dec9a496038197f369091daec82af3","clm_83588e36928427d7e20021b8153c665ff1b59d50beac42fb2faf24404ea9beea","clm_915110b53b566041c048c8578b226d2d84a2347d511aa977e073d9667ab4b760","clm_9813c92cc8a5d7265e9f2d1e9767c0b515cc229ad39154aebb9da2144e7e5dcf"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:04:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_c3b68b30a908496abe5ab36586526291","id":"pg_95b6097c2ec750a8884012724760cc0d","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/hotovo-aider-desk-docs-adr-readme-md-cb7ee89bf213-12724760cc0d.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_529c6745829e5cb1b9dc7574eca57036"],"title":"hotovo/aider-desk/docs/adr/README.md @ cb7ee89bf213","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:04:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_c3b68b30a908496abe5ab36586526291"}
